WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.720
Gemini Man's intriguing premise isn't necessarily
new, but the Ang Lee-directed sci-fi thriller

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:10.620
presents a number of chances to look at a
familiar story in ways that other movies haven't.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.740
These are just some of the implications left
hanging by the end of the film - and what

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.510
they mean for the people left standing.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.570
Even before he realizes that he's unwittingly
been roped into a massive conspiracy involving

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:27.820
a secret cloning program and a clone of himself
growing up right under his nose, Will Smith's

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.400
Henry Brogan is tired.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:34.120
He finds himself slowing down, losing his
touch, and more importantly, he's beginning

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.020
to struggle with his job a little more.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.920
Killing people is no longer a satisfying bit
of service to his country.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.860
It's something he struggles to live with.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.800
The journey of Gemini Man is Henry's journey
to quite literally contend with himself and

00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:50.710
his place in the world, and he comes out the
other side of it feeling a little better about

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:51.200
himself.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.760
His defeat of Gemini leader Clay Varris allows
him to sleep a little easier at night, he

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.229
admits he can finally look in a mirror, and
he's found a surrogate son who just happens

00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:03.300
to share his exact DNA profile in Junior.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.520
Henry Brogan's killer instinct might not go
away overnight, and neither will his guilt

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:12.050
or any traces of post-traumatic stress, but
he has people in his life who care about him

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.980
at last, and that's a good start.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:19.280
We get less character development on the side
of "Junior," Henry Brogan's young clone who

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.850
was adopted as Clay Varris' son, but we know
enough to understand that he's got a tough

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.850
road ahead of him.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:29.590
Junior was created to be the ultimate killer,
a man with all of Brogan's natural skills

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.860
and athleticism but none of the emotional
issues he grew up with.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.340
In talking with Junior, Henry revealed that
Clay's attempts at taking all of those issues

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.960
away from Junior didn't work.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:43.700
The young clone still struggles with issues
of inadequacy, with nightmares, and with struggling

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.680
to find joy anywhere besides on the other
side of a gun.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.180
"I’m guessing 19, 20 years old the first
time he ordered you to shoot a person?”

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.020
By the end of the film, Junior - renamed Jackson
Brogan at his request - has found some degree

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.740
of actual, tangible joy in his life, and most
of it comes in the form of choice.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.240
He seems genuinely happy at the end of the
film, but this isn't the end of his struggles.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.319
He's dealing with the weight of psychological
trauma sustained throughout his relationship

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:16.210
with his adoptive father, but thankfully,
he's got people in his corner to help him

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:16.700
out.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.180
From the moment we meet her in the film, Mary
Elizabeth Winstead's Danny proves to be a

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.400
resourceful and sharp DIA operative.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:29.240
Over the course of Gemini Man, she keeps proving
that she's always cool under pressure, despite

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:33.129
being propelled into one of the most improbable
situations of her career.

00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:37.459
By the end of the film, Danny and Henry are
close friends, and Danny has even become at

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.520
least somewhat close to Jackson Brogan, Henry's
young clone.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.300
More than that, though, she reveals that she's
been promoted within the DIA, a likely result

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:49.120
of the restructuring that had to take place
once the Gemini cloning project was brought

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.000
to light and ultimately dismantled.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.100
That puts Danny in a position to not just
help Henry and Jackson as they try to get

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.380
on with their lives, but to hopefully prevent
anyone from meddling in Jackson's future as

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:03.760
he tries to simply enjoy his 20s, free from
the life of an assassin.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.800
At one point in the film, Henry and his old
Marine buddy Baron are talking about their

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.269
history with Clay Varris.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.240
They both recount how he asked them to join
up with his new venture and how they both

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:14.860
declined.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.100
Baron, in fact, said no and then moved to
a different continent, putting him at least

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.760
somewhat out of Varris' reach.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.019
Henry stayed in America, and later found out
that Varris had used his blood to create a

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.560
perfect supersoldier clone.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.340
As the film unfolds, we learn more and more
about the dark dealings of Gemini, including

00:03:31.349 --> 00:03:36.010
the last-minute revelation that Varris created
at least one more clone of Henry and managed

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.520
to edit out his sense of pain.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.599
By the time the film is over, Henry's old
friend Del assures him that the Gemini lab

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.400
has been shuttered, hopefully putting an end
to Varris' secretive dealings.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.000
Any fan of spy movies knows that it can't
possibly be that simple, though.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.080
The film leaves us hanging, but there has
to be something more.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.820
So we know that Junior was cloned from a sample
of Henry's blood more than two decades earlier,

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.500
and he was raised from infancy by Clay Varris.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.959
At some point in the intervening years, Varris
took that endeavor a step further and cloned

00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:10.260
Henry again, this time drafting a top scientist
to edit out things like pain sensitivity from

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:12.040
the second clone's genetic code.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.800
"Look what we created.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.373
You were the inspiration for all of this."

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.800
"Why not just make a whole army full of them?"

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:25.200
So, Gemini Man posits a world in which a rich
paramilitary contractor has had viable cloning

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.870
technology in his hands for more than 20 years,
and in that time, he's found a way to breed

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.940
supersoldiers that don't feel pain.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:33.720
What else has he figured out?

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:38.400
How many other scientists has he spoken to,
and perhaps most importantly, who else has

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.960
access to this technology?

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.310
Now that Varris is dead, is someone else going
to finish what he started?

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:48.480
If there's a sequel to Gemini Man, that seems
like fertile ground to explore.

